# BH-7636: this box runs the lane_runs rows placed on it. A project row lane_placement.<lane>.<project> = box:<this box's hostname, fleet.conf col 6> (lanes merge-conductor and fly-pool) sends that (lane, project) to this box, and the jobs worker hands those rows only to a claim that names it. The hub enqueues the row and runs no tick of that project; this line claims and runs it (bin/merge-conductor-project.sh or bin/fly-pool-project.sh, under the project lease). With no row placed here the claim answers 204 and this line does nothing. Undo: set the row to hub. flock -n: one worker at a time, never a queue.
# BH-7716: a registered lane (catalog/lanes.d/lane-run-box.json, boxes [project-6-os]); bin/lane-run-box.sh gates on lane-off-lane-run-box and then execs bin/lane-run-worker.sh with these arguments.
* * * * * flock -n /root/harness/locks/lane-run-box.lock /root/harness/bin/lane-run-box.sh --once --box "$(hostname)" >> /root/harness/logs/lane-run-box-cron.log 2>&1
